From f5093737c16957e3e42353b9550c0e11c1adc9fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:37:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] generate: STRATA_ADMIT_MERGE_FIRST=1 reads a batch
 admission's last prompt tokens and its first token in one window

A batch admission read its header through the verify windows (T=4 + T=2 for the
usual 6 tokens) and then its first token in a window of the last prompt token
alone. With the switch the last windowed part leaves its last tokens (up to the
verifier's max_t, 8, the last prompt token included) to the first window: the
part's earlier tokens are read as before, the first window commits every row,
the drafter gets the rows of the prompt tokens in it as the prompt windows give
them, and only row T-1's output is emitted. Row T-1 sits at the first window's
position with the same history and Philox draw, and a row computes what it
computes in any window while every expert is in VRAM, so the token and the
state are the same.

Only for a BGEN admission with every expert of every stage in VRAM (no loan,
no swap pending, the zero-doorbell graphs), and not with --batch-mtp, the
pipelined windows, pictures, the elastic K/V, a peer device, remote caches,
foresight swaps, STRATA_LOGPOS or a checkpoint at the last token. The merged
window takes no drafter q (STRATA_SPEC_PROB), adds nothing to the draft
counts, and the "PP <n-1>" line is printed before it. Verifier::max_t() is new.

Off by default: the same path as before. Tokens (4x RTX 3090, split
12,24,36, 16 slots, STRATA_IQ_MT_MIN=1): 24 admissions of prompts of 3 to 65
tokens and chat headers with and without an assistant prefill (merged T 3 to
8), greedy, seeded and with penalties, on vs off identical; batch_test16 16/16
and equal to the earlier dump; batch_overlap_test token- and RESUME-identical;
batch_interleave_test equal; 47 sampled driver requests equal.

Measured (24 admissions, ~131 and ~1195 tokens): header windows 23.5 plus
first window 11.5 ms become one 7-token window of 27.6 ms, 7.4 ms less per
admission (send to first batch token 246.8 -> 239.4 ms short, 656.1 -> 648.5
long). A window row costs ~2.4 ms up to T=6 and ~4 ms at T=7 and 8 (T=1 11.4,
T=7 28.6, T=8 32.1 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
